yosys: techmap maps cells in the order of their names' characters

techmap_module() put a module's cells in a TopoSort ordered by
IdString::compare_ptr_by_name, that is by IdString::operator<, which
compares interning indices. The indices depend on which names the rest
of the design holds or held: the same module, synthesized on its own or
inside its design, or after another module was freed, got its cells
mapped in another order. The order reaches the output: the cells are
reinserted into the module in that order, which later passes iterate,
and techmap's own autoidx-based names ($techmap<n>, NEW_ID wires) are
handed out in it. Two flows that give a module byte-identical RTLIL
before techmap gave it different netlists after.

The TopoSort now orders cells by IdString::lt_by_name, the name's
characters, as techmap already orders its templates (sort_by_id_str).

Upstream candidate for YosysHQ/yosys; not filed. Carried by bazel-orfs
as yosys-0007 with its test, yosys-0008. Retires at the bump onto a
BCR yosys that orders techmap's cells by name.

--- a/passes/techmap/techmap.cc
+++ b/passes/techmap/techmap.cc
@@ -39,6 +39,16 @@
 USING_YOSYS_NAMESPACE
 PRIVATE_NAMESPACE_BEGIN
 
+// Cells are mapped in this order and the order reaches the autoidx-based
+// names techmap gives, so it is by the name's characters: IdString's
+// operator< compares interning indices, which depend on the names the rest
+// of the design holds or held.
+struct CompareCellByNameStr {
+	bool operator()(const RTLIL::Cell *a, const RTLIL::Cell *b) const {
+		return a->name.lt_by_name(b->name);
+	}
+};
+
 void apply_prefix(IdString prefix, IdString &id)
 {
 	if (id[0] == '\\')
@@ -424,7 +434,7 @@
 		SigMap sigmap(module);
 		FfInitVals initvals(&sigmap, module);
 
-		TopoSort<RTLIL::Cell*, IdString::compare_ptr_by_name<RTLIL::Cell>> cells;
+		TopoSort<RTLIL::Cell*, CompareCellByNameStr> cells;
 		dict<RTLIL::Cell*, pool<RTLIL::SigBit>> cell_to_inbit;
 		dict<RTLIL::SigBit, pool<RTLIL::Cell*>> outbit_to_cell;
 
